{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And He said</b> — the word יהי is יהיה. Because it is spoken of often, it is both singular and plural, and also feminine: \"כי יהיה נערה בתולה\" (Deuteronomy 22:23)." "For signs — moments; and for seasons — hours. And it is possible that לאותות refers to the darkening of the moon and the sun, and the leap-formations of the stars, for the stars are the cause of the visible forms, as in the sense of מאותות השמים אל תחתו (Jeremiah 10:2). And he who says that the lamed of לאותות is superfluous has said nothing." "<b>And they shall be for signs</b> — a great sage of Spain said that the rakia is divided into eight parts for the seven planets and the zodiac sphere, and this is impossible, for there is no body above the zodiac sphere, and behold Scripture says ברקיע השמים, which indicates that there are heavens above it, and likewise שמי השמים (Nehemiah 9:6), לרוכב בשמי שמי קדם (Psalms 68:34) — and קדם in this place is not east, and the Gaon [Saadia] fled from this passage, and the correct view in my eyes is that the sun and the moon and all the stars are lights in the rakia, for there they are seen."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "The word דלוג is taken as 'leaping' or 'skipping' formations of the stars, reading it as a technical term; the phrase remains cryptic as per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:41.543395849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}